<h1 class="visually-hidden">A Little Bit of Gore</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Sound design, music &amp; implementation &middot; 2024 &middot; free on itch.io</p>

<p>Little Bit of Gore is a short first-person survival horror game by Matthew Ganther. You're a tiny mushroom, newly sprouted into a world drowned in gore, and you have to find five glowing mushrooms while mutated bugs hunt you through the long grass.</p>
<p>Hearing the monsters is how you stay alive, so the sound is a big part of how the game plays. I designed and implemented its sound effects, ambience and music in FMOD and Unreal Engine 5; fellow student Ryan did the sound for the intro animation.</p>

{% video { youtube: "EI_Ai8QRa8k", title: "A Little Bit of Gore audio showcase", caption: "Audio showcase: the monsters, the music and the ambience in the game." } %}

<h2>What I did</h2>
<ul class="points">
  <li>A sound for each monster that tells you where it is and what it's about to do</li>
  <li>An adaptive score in four layers, and a three-layer ambience</li>
  <li>Footsteps, the menus and the intro screen</li>
  <li>Implementation in FMOD Studio and Unreal Engine 5.1, including an occlusion system</li>
</ul>

<h2>The monsters</h2>
<ul class="points">
  <li><b>Stalker</b> follows you and strikes when its time runs out, unless you turn and look at it. Its breathing is me bowing metal rulers on the Apprehension Engine (a horror-sound instrument at RMIT), layered with my own wails and a low hum. A tremolo speeds up as it gets ready to strike, so you can hear when to turn around. Its whispers are four reversed takes of me whispering "s", drowned in reverb and reverse delay.</li>
  <li><b>The Bug Monstrosity</b> hunts you down like a Pac-Man ghost, so it's loud and repetitive: easy to track, and to avoid.</li>
  <li><b>The Infected Mushroom</b> charges in bursts, then sleeps. Its footsteps are boosted hard in the sub-bass, with more reverb the further away it is, so you feel it coming.</li>
  <li><b>The Ants</b> scuttle about and shriek when you get too close.</li>
</ul>

