<h2>Music and ambience</h2>
<p>The score is an ambient horror piece in four layers, written with Kontakt in RMIT's 5.1 studio. The first three build as you collect mushrooms; the fourth comes in when the Infected Mushroom or the Bug Monstrosity gets close. Underneath, the ambience has three layers of its own: soft wind through the crops, a howling wind, and a distant, echoing voice every 30 to 90 seconds, a hint that something much bigger is out there.</p>

{% soundcloud { track: "1820216838", title: "Little Bit of Gore score intensities", caption: "The score's four levels of intensity, one after another." } %}

<h2>Implementation</h2>
<p>In FMOD and Unreal Engine 5.1 I built an occlusion system that muffles and quietens any monster behind a wall or a row of crops, so you can tell where it really is, and an intensity system that raises the music and ambience as you collect mushrooms. The footsteps are me stepping in a bucket of soil, cut into a seamless loop.</p>

